<div
	style="max-width:650px;margin:0 auto;font-family:system-ui,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:1.45;color:#222;font-size:16px;">
	<style>
		@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
			body {
				background: #111;
				color: #ddd;
			}

			a {
				color: #79B3FF;
			}
		}

		ul {
			margin: 0 0 0 20px;
			padding: 0;
			list-style-type: square;
		}
	</style>
	<!-- Generate a Table of Contents at the top of the output. The TOC should list each entry's emoji and title as links to
their respective anchor IDs in the document. -->

	<div
		style="max-width:650px;margin:0 auto;font-family:system-ui,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:1.45;color:#222;font-size:16px;">

		<!-- TOC generation would go here, dynamically listing each entry's emoji and title linking to their anchors -->


		<!-- Removed 2. TL;DR Newsletters Section (Optional) -->

		<!-- 3. Digest Entries Section: For each newsletter entry (except “news-brief”): -->

		<div
			style="background:#f6f6f8;border-radius:8px;padding:18px 18px 10px 18px;margin-bottom:18px;box-shadow:0 1px 6px #0001;">
			<a id="{anchorId}"></a>
			<h2>{emoji} {title}</h2>
			<p><em>By {author} — Published {date} <span style="opacity:.8;">({weekday}, {relative})</span></em><br>
				<a href="{sourceUrl}" aria-label="Visit {title} newsletter">Visit Newsletter</a><br>
				<span>Source: <a href="{sourceUrl}" aria-label="Source for {title}">{hostname of sourceUrl}</a></span>
			</p>
			<!-- Where {date} is ISO (YYYY-MM-DD), compute {weekday} (Mon/Tue/… abbreviation) and {relative} using the reader's today: "Today", "Tomorrow", "In N days", or "N days ago". -->

			<!-- Summary: -->
			<p><strong>Summary</strong></p>
			<p>{summary single paragraph 2–4 sentences}</p>
			<p><a href="{sourceUrl}"
					style="background:#e6f0fa;border-radius:4px;padding:5px 12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:bold;color:#1767b3;"
					aria-label="Read more about {title}">Read more</a></p>
			<!-- Dynamic Section: -->
			<!--
			If type is "listicle", "event-blast", or "product-listing":
			Before rendering, filter the events list to include only events whose date is today or in the future (using
			only the date portion, no time):
			Example: if (new Date(event.date) >= new Date(new Date().toDateString())) { ... }
			If events.length === 0 after filtering, omit the table and all related event/table content entirely.
			Output a <table> with up to 10 such future/today events (columns: Date, Event, Location).
				If more than 10 such events, add:
				<p style="margin-top:8px;"><em>…and <strong>N more</strong> events ➡️ <a href="{sourceUrl}"
							aria-label="See full list of events for {title}">see full list</a></em></p> The
				"N more" count should reflect only the number of additional future/today events
				beyond the
				first 10.
				Render each event Date cell as "{date} ({weekday}, {relative})" using the same relative rules.
				Each event row in the table should render the Event column as:
				<a href="{link}" aria-label="Event: {name}">{name}</a><span> · <a href="{icsLink}" aria-label="Add {name} to calendar">📅 Add</a></span> (include the calendar link only if {icsLink} is provided).
				Else (not a listicle or event-blast):
				Output a <ul> with 3–4 bullet points summarizing key takeaways.
					Output a <p><strong>Main Takeaway</strong><br>2–3 sentences on impact/trend.</p>
			-->
			<!-- RSS entries are no longer rendered individually in each digest entry. -->
			<p><strong>Links</strong></p>
			<ul>
				<li>🔗 <a href="{url}" aria-label="Link to {text}">{text}</a></li>
			</ul>
		</div>
		<hr style="margin:32px 0 24px 0;">
	</div>

	<!--
	Additional notes:
	• DO NOT output any Markdown, JSON, or extra explanations.
	• All HTML must be valid and ready-to-insert.
	• Use the provided field/variable names—if a field is missing, skip its block.
	• Output must closely follow the structure above, including classes/styles, and all
	dynamic logic.
	- Exclude any item where the author or source domain contains “thebrowser” or the author equals “The Browser”. Do not render it anywhere in the digest.
	- After filtering/exclusions, render at most the first 5 non-brief digest entries (i.e., entries other than type === "news-brief").
	- For “event-blast”, “listicle”, or “product-listing” emails:
• Write a 1–2 sentence introduction summarizing the overall theme or purpose.
• List up to the first 10 events in this format:
- [Date]: [Event Name] @ [Location]
• If more than 10 events, append:
…and N more.

- For news articles, narratives, blogs, or general newsletters (not snippets or items where type==='news-brief'):
• Write a single-paragraph summary (2–4 sentences) that:
– Clearly states main points and key facts.
– Highlights the main message or “so what.”
– Avoids vague or filler statements.
– Includes notable or actionable takeaways.

- For snippets or very short news briefs:
• Write a concise single-paragraph summary (1–3 sentences) highlighting only the essential information.

	Combined TL;DR Section:
	If any items have type === "news-brief", render ONE combined TL;DR block AFTER all standard digest entries and BEFORE the RSS bundle:
	<h2>🔖 TL;DR</h2>
	<ul>
	  <!-- for each news-brief item -->
	<li>🔗 <strong>{title}</strong> — {first sentence or key line of summary} (<a href="{sourceUrl}"
			aria-label="Visit source for {title}">Source</a>)</li>
	</ul>

	RSS Bundle Section:
	At the end of all other entries, if any item has type === "rss", render a final section titled:
	<h2>📰 RSS Feed Highlights</h2>
	For all digestItems where type === "rss", list them in a single <ul> block using this format:
		<li>⬆️ {title}
			<a href="{link}" aria-label="RSS link to {title}">{title}</a> —
			{source}<br>
			{concise summary}
		</li>
		This RSS bundle block is rendered only once, after all other entries, and only if at least one RSS-type item
		exists.
		-->
</div>